{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in: 4.4.dev7 [46c8f8c5c]\n-Not reproducible in 4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev7 - macOS Sequoia (15.2.0) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M1 Pro (Apple7) - Apple M1 Pro (10 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn last dev7 build if we have no projects, it's possible to import a project but disable the \"Edit Now\" checkbox, this causes the window to not refresh properly and we end up in a state where it shows the project but the \"No projects\" message still show up\n\nIf we import with \"Edit Now\" disabled\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33c740bb-60ab-44c7-9ab3-91712fe36cba)\n\nIt shows the project but also the existing message.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5eaaf485-5cd4-4056-bf84-12cc4fb35934)\n\nThis would not happen in 4.3 because we were always forced to Edit it. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3c7d6bd-7fe3-4c3e-8a0e-5156dbb960d1)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Boot Godot\n- In the project manager, and with no projects listed (remove if any) try to import one but deselect \"Edit Now\"\n- Notice the message of \"No projects\" still shows but the imported project is now on the list as well\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github